# enclave llama.cpp patch - device top-k rows (mm26).
#
# Backend sampling could serve at most ONE output row per sequence, which
# made it useless for the speculative verify (one sequence, k+1 output
# rows). This patch:
#   1. lifts that restriction: build_sampling instantiates the sampler
#      chain once per OUTPUT ROW, and the result maps are keyed by the
#      local output row (the key type stays int32; the async copies and
#      the _ith getters were row-indexed already);
#   2. bounds the sampler graph by output-row count (LLAMA_SAMPLER_MAX_ROWS,
#      default 8): wider batches - prefill chunks - take the raw-logits
#      path unchanged, needs_raw_logits mirrors the bound;
#   3. stores a chain's output logits only when a sampler REDUCED them
#      (top_k's K-sized gather): greedy used to leave the full-vocab input
#      view in llama_sampler_data.logits, and the copy of that row (~1 MB,
#      forced-sync under CC) was silently taxing the mm24 head chains;
#   4. drops the dummy-row pad + inactive-sampler applications: graph
#      slots are keyed by (n_tokens, seq) on this engine (graph-slot
#      patch), so sampler topology is a function of the slot key, and the
#      stability trick only cost a full-vocab sort per idle sequence.
#
# With a [top_k(K)] chain armed on the serving context (the shim's
# ENCLAVE_GGML_DEV_TOPK), a k=1 verify reads back 2 x K ids+logits instead
# of extracting 2 x 248320 floats through the CC-forced-synchronous D2H
# and scanning them on SNP-throttled vCPUs. Requires GGML_CUDA_USE_CUB
# for wide-row CUDA TOP_K (auto-on at CUDA >= 11.7; the toolchain builds
# with 12.4).
#
# Applies AFTER llamacpp-rs-pin-cells.patch (diffed against the patched
# tree). Kill switch: leave ENCLAVE_GGML_DEV_TOPK unset - with no chains
# armed every path is byte-for-byte stock.
